From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 21:21:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: msm8998-google-taimen: drop the PD on the
 voice services

The four audio services already drop qcom,protection-domain here because
this ADSP firmware does not host "avs/audio": the locator answers but
never lists the service, so the lookup never completes.

MVM, CVS and CVP inherit the same property from the SoC dtsi and need
the same treatment. Without it apr_probe() registers only the services
that have no protection domain, and the three voice services are never
added to the bus at all -- visible as /sys/bus/aprbus/devices holding
4:3, 4:4, 4:7 and 4:8 and nothing else.

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998-google-taimen.dts | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998-google-taimen.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998-google-taimen.dts
index 8c9b425015d3..dc2a413cf8bc 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998-google-taimen.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998-google-taimen.dts
@@ -451,6 +451,18 @@ &q6adm {
 	/delete-property/ qcom,protection-domain;
 };
 
+&q6mvm {
+	/delete-property/ qcom,protection-domain;
+};
+
+&q6cvs {
+	/delete-property/ qcom,protection-domain;
+};
+
+&q6cvp {
+	/delete-property/ qcom,protection-domain;
+};
+
 /*
  * The audio DSP reaches its PCM buffers only through this SMMU. With it
  * disabled the q6asm dais device gets no IOMMU group, falls back to direct
